\ A user-defined combinator of the `times` shape, recursing by name so the
\ recursion routes through the generic self-tail-call path (not the inline
\ `times` emitter). The body calls `2dip` on its quotation parameter, collapsing
\ the abstract stack to a bounded row with the counter and quotation threaded
\ above it. Built under runtime-image AOT, the row-aware self-tail-call back-edge
\ compiles the combinator body to a native loop; the quotation parameter still
\ runs through the interpreter, and the printed output matches the interpreter.
my-times: ( n quot -- ) [
  over 0 >
  [ dup 2dip swap -- swap my-times ]
  [ 2drop ]
  if
] ;

3 [ "tick" print-line ] my-times
0 [ "skip" print-line ] my-times
"done" print-line
